  "details": "Can't upload without having to restart Unity after importing the newest SDK3, making people think that there could be stuff wrong when they e.g. buy an avatar and want to upload it.\nWhen doing the following:\n1. setting up a new project with Unity2019.4.31f1\n2. importing latest SDK3 (VRCSDK3-AVATAR-2022.04.26.15.46_Public)\n-> throws a few errors due to missing packages as explained by VRChat:\n```\n# SDK\nThe SDK now requires that the Burst and Mathematics packages are installed. If they aren't installed, the SDK will install them for you on import. This may result in errors during first installation, but they will go away after a restart or a log clear.\n```\nAfterwards, importing the following (as defined per package dependencies):\n3. import PoiToon 7.0.46 (bundled with pretty much any v8 release of the past months)\n4. import db 1.3.2\n5. import avatar package and opening the setup scene\n6. upload\nThrows the errors as seen in the attached picture.\n\nYou can simply restart the project after the failed upload and it'll work - unity has to properly install the packages because it doesn't automatically do it, a log clear does not prevent the errors in the upload process unless you've restarted the project.\nI'd assume you could also import the lastest SDK3 and restart your project right afterwards and an upload should work rightaway.\n\nIs there anything that can be done about that e.g. automating the import and instalation of the necessary packages or telling the people to restart the project to get it to work? It's a bit frustrating trying to troubleshoot this when ppl are following the instructions of how to set up certain avatar packages and think something's wrong on their or the distributor's end.",
